      "loggedRequestAttempts": 1,
      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 138,
      "outputTokens": 982,
      "costUsd": 0.008907,
      "pronunciationText": "What happens when the curve crosses the axis? Stretch the same curve out to three. It crosses at two, and from two to three it's above the axis. That piece has integral seven thirds. Now the whole integral, from zero to three, is minus three. And minus three is seven thirds, minus sixteen thirds. So the integral is the area above the axis, minus the area below it. That's the lift's net change, floors up minus floors down. But it's not the area. For the area, like the floors travelled, take each piece on its own and make it positive. Sixteen thirds plus seven thirds is twenty-three thirds."
    },
