      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 167,
      "outputTokens": 1269,
      "costUsd": 0.0115045,
      "pronunciationText": "Often there's no graph. Find the area bounded by y equals x squared minus four x plus three, the x-axis, and the lines x equals zero and x equals four. First, find where the curve meets the axis. It factorises as x minus one, times x minus three, so the zeros are one and three. They split the interval into three pieces. Test a value in each piece. At zero, y is three, positive. At two, y is minus one, negative. At four, y is three, positive. Now integrate each piece. The answers are four thirds, minus four thirds, and four thirds. Make each one positive and add, so the area is four. The single integral from zero to four is only four thirds, because the middle piece cancels one of the others."
    },
