      "inputTokens": 125,
      "outputTokens": 894,
      "costUsd": 0.0081085,
      "pronunciationText": "This difference has a meaning when the graph is a velocity. Take the car with velocity twelve minus two t metres per second, from zero to eight seconds. Its integral is thirty-two metres. That's the displacement, where the car ends up compared with where it started. But the car stops at six seconds and then reverses. Forward from zero to six, it travels thirty-six metres. From six to eight, the integral is minus four, so it travels four metres back. The total distance is thirty-six plus four, which is forty metres. Displacement is the signed integral. Distance is the area."
    },
